<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    ARM vcmp/vmrs and AArch64 fcmp set NZCV=0011 for unordered operands, so
    each condition code decides a NaN its own way: gt and ge are false for
    it, le, lt and hi are true. P3 nanignore folding
    (kuna_floatnegation.rs fold_exact_conditions) evaluates the flag
    expression for every ordering of the two operands, NaNs included, and
    keeps the one comparison it equals before the NaN test is dropped.
    Strict correctness fix, no option: the one pass is the fix.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture. The script loads
    four in-tree fixtures (sources beside them). fcmp_unordered_a64.o reads
    every AArch64 condition by cset after fcmp d0,d1, one after fcmp s0,#0.0,
    and branches with b.le. fcmp_unordered_a32.o branches on six ARM
    conditions after vcmp.f64 d0,d1 and vmrs. scale_err (clang -O2) branches
    with ble against 88.0f, logish (clang, Thumb) on a compare with 0.0f, and
    ccw_mixed reads cset gt after fcmp d0,#0.0.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
